    {
        "content": "<p>avanhatt opened <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/13998\">PR #13998</a> from <code>avanhatt:veri-spec-type-check</code> to <code>bytecodealliance:main</code>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Type check term specs in isolation, and fix the over-constrained specs it finds.</p>\n<p>Adds a check that type-checks verification conditions for each term used in an ISLE compilation one at a time, against nothing but its own declared types, so that a genuine type conflict is distinct from an expansion that shouldn't be reached for a specific type.</p>\n<p>The one gnarly case is the spec for <code>aarch64</code> <code>MInst.MovFromVec</code>: because <code>aarch64</code> does not have separate <code>Reg</code> types for distinct sizes, it's difficult to faithfully model 128-bit-registers via our <code>aslp</code> automatically generated specs. Adds a special case to only <code>spec</code> the low 64-bits of the register and leave the top unconstrained (sound, but incomplete).</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 613050200,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1785179029
    },
